    "body": "My first question here would be, why `translatable-data-*` and not `data-translatable-*`? With the former there'd be an expectation for a JS accessor like `.translatableDataset` to be introduced, to match the existing [`.dataset`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLElement/dataset). With the latter, JS code could continue to use `.dataset` and the only change you'd actually be asking for the prefix to be listed as a translatable attribute.\n\nSecond, I don't think it's very common to attach `data-*` attributes on custom elements, so the usage there seems like a bit of a stretch. Rather, it seems like you're pointing at an inability to easily signal the translatability of attributes on custom elements, and that while that problem would be ameliorated by making `data-translatable-*` attributes translatable, it's not necessarily the only or best solution for them.",
