    "body": "> > If so, maybe, but that violates the spec so I don't want to encourage it further.\n> \n> I would be _very_ surprised if it turned out that using completely custom attributes on a custom element were not completely fine.\n\nIt's \"fine\" until it isn't. The reason the `data-*` namespace is carved out is to preserve the platform's ability to add attributes, such as the `popover` global attribute. That attribute was originally called `popup` but that broke the web because authors were already using it. That's bad for the platform.",
