    "body": "```js\nthis.attachShadow({mode: 'open'}).innerHTML = `<span>${this.dataset.text}</span>`;\n```\n\nIs this actually in need of a new attribute? Wouldn't this already work, as it's text in the DOM?\n\nAs for the CSS content property shouldn't that basically always be translated? This doesn't solve the case where authors just put strings in their content property, those still need translating?\n\n------------\n\nI'm unsure if there is a need for this, *but* if there is:\n\nI'm personally against these attributes starting with `data-translatable-*` the data prefix is specifically for entirely custom author attributes and I don't think we should step that on that. `translatable-data` seems probably fine, but maybe just dropping data entirely would be good?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
